"Internal Error ()\nciteturn156view0 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://github.com/xSyllaa/sunflower-pendant-chain\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\nL0: Failed to fetch https://github.com/xSyllaa/sunflower-pendant-chain: Cache miss\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nECCC - TR26-220 (https://eccc.weizmann.ac.il/report/2026/220/)\nciteturn156view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://eccc.weizmann.ac.il/report/2026/220/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 51\nL0: 【0†Image: Electronic Colloquium on Computational Complexity】\nL1: \nL2: Under the auspices of the 【1†Computational Complexity Foundation (CCF)†computationalcomplexity.org】\nL3: \nL4: [Input] [Input]\nL5: \nL6: 【2†Image: |】 【2†Image: |】\nL7: \nL8: 【3†Image: icon】 【4†Image: Submit Paper】\nL9:   *   *   *     *     * 【5†2026】\nL10:     * 【6†2025】\nL11:     * 【7†2024】\nL12:     * 【8†2026...1994】\nL13:     *   *   *     *     *     *     *     *     *   *     * 【9†Call for Papers】\nL14:     * 【10†How to use】\nL15:     * 【11†Scientific Board】\nL16:     * 【12†Local Office】\nL17:     * 【13†Copyright Notice】\nL18:     * 【14†History】\nL19:   *     *     *     *     *     *     *   *     *     *     *     *     *     *   * * * *\nL20: \nL21: REPORTS > DETAIL:\nL22: \nL23: * * *\nL24: ### Paper:\nL25: \nL26: TR26-220 | 28th September 2026 17:29\nL27: #### Derandomized Sunflowers and Radical Lower Bounds\nL28: \nL29: 【15†Image: Contact】\nL30: \nL31: 【16†Image: Add Comment】\nL32: \nL33: 【17†TR26-220】 Authors: 【18†Bruno Pasqualotto Cavalar】, 【19†Théo Fabris】, 【20†Partha Mukhopadhyay】, 【21†Srikanth Srinivasan】, 【22†Amir Yehudayoff】\nL34: Publication: 28th September 2026 18:10\nL35: Downloads: 554\nL36: \nL37: Keywords:\nL38: \nL39: 【23†Derandomization of Robust Sunflower lemmas】, 【24†Monotone Arithmetic Circuits】, 【25†monotone Boolean circuits】, 【26†Nisan-Wigderson designs】, 【27†the method of moments】\nL40: \nL41: Abstract:\nL42: Robust Sunflower lemmas imply that any large enough monotone DNF of width $w$ contains a sunflower, i.e., a DNF equivalent to the conjunction of a common core with a DNF that is heavily biased towards $1$. While these lemmas are typically proved in the context of the uniform distribution or i.i.d.\nL43: distributions, they also hold for $O(w^2)$-wise independent distributions by Bazzi's theorem (Bazzi (SICOMP 2009); Tal (CCC 2017)), which states that width-$w$ DNFs cannot distinguish between such distributions and the uniform distribution.\nL44: We prove a derandomization of robust sunflower lemmas for $O(w)$-wise independent distributions, which recovers the derandomization above with slightly weaker parameters. Notably, our result also holds for distributions whose marginals are \"locally independent\" and \"approximately identically\" distributed. It is not known whether such distributions fool general DNFs, which makes the derandomization via DNF-fooling techniques unavailable.\nL45: Our proof of this derandomization is via the method of moments, which might be of independent interest.\nL46: We apply this result to obtain improved separations between non-monotone arithmetic circuits and the radical of monotone circuits. Specifically, we construct an \\emph{explicit} family of multilinear polynomials $P_n$ that have small non-monotone arithmetic circuits such that any power of $P_n$ cannot be computed by monotone arithmetic circuits of \\emph{sub-exponential} size.\nL47: This improves on a recent result of Cavalar, Fabris, Mukhopadhyay, Srinivasan and Yehudayoff (STOC 2026), who proved a non-explicit separation that was quasipolynomial. Our construction uses Nisan-Wigderson designs with an additional linear-algebraic expansion property.\nL48: * * *\nL49: \nL50: ISSN 1433-8092 | 【28†Imprint】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2610.26686] Proof of the Erdős-Szemerédi sunflower conjecture (https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.26686)\nciteturn156view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.26686\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 159\nL0: 【0†Search】 【1†Submit】 【2†Donate†info.arxiv.org】 【3†Log in】\nL1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · 【4†Advanced search】\nL5: \nL6: # Mathematics > Combinatorics\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 19 Oct 2026]\nL9: # Title:Proof of the Erdős-Szemerédi sunflower conjecture\nL10: \nL11: Authors:【5†Matija Bucić】, 【6†Fankang He】, 【7†Hyunwoo Lee】\nL12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Proof of the Erd\\H{o}s-Szemer\\'edi sunflower conjecture, by Matija Buci\\'c and 2 other authors\nL14: \nL15: 【8†View PDF】 【9†HTML (experimental)】\nL16: > Abstract:In the 1970s, Erdős and Szemerédi conjectured that for any $n \\ge k-1\\ge 2$, any collection of subsets of $[n]$ not containing a $k$-sunflower has size at most $c_k^n$ for some $c_k<2$. In the $k=3$ case, this follows from the work of Croot, Lev, and Pach and Ellenberg and Gijswijt on the cap-set problem, through a reduction due to Alon, Shpilka, and Umans. We prove the conjecture for every $k \\ge 3$.\nL17: Subjects:  | Combinatorics (math.CO)\nL18: Cite as:  | 【10†arXiv:2610.26686】 [math.CO]\nL19:    | (or 【11†arXiv:2610.26686v1】 [math.CO] for this version)\nL20:    | 【12†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2610.26686†doi.org】 arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL21: ## Submission history\nL22: \nL23: From: Matija Bucic [【13†view email】]\nL24: [v1] Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:32:32 UTC (32 KB)\nL25: \nL26: Full-text links:\nL27: \nL28: ## Access Paper:\nL29: \nL30: View a PDF of the paper titled Proof of the Erd\\H{o}s-Szemer\\'edi sunflower conjecture, by Matija Buci\\'c and 2 other authors\nL31: \nL32:   * 【8†View PDF】\nL33:   * 【9†HTML (experimental)】\nL34:   * 【14†TeX Source】\nL35: \nL36: 【15†view license】\nL37: \nL38: ### Current browse cont